From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:47:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 203/225] cpufreq: sprd-hwdvfs: switch MPLL output to DVFS
 control before relock/pd

Both CPU clusters stay parked on their TWPLL boot parent (A55 at 1536MHz,
A75 at 1228.8MHz) even though every DVFS register reads correct: the work
index latches, the voltage path responds, all enables are set and all three
MPLLs are released from software control. Sampling the block across a real
driver->set shows MPLL_DVFS_STATE (0x322a82a0) and APCPU_FREQ_UPDATE_STATE0
(0x322a82a4) never leave zero, so the frequency-update state machine is
never triggered at all.

The vendor 5.4 driver keeps this bit-clear as a distinct step,
sprd_mpll_output_source_switch(), and calls it first in its per-MPLL init
loop, ahead of auto relock and auto power down, followed by a 50us wait for
"finishing analog configuration". Our 4.14-derived copy does the same clear
inline but only after relock and pd are already enabled, and without the
settle delay.

Reorder to match the vendor sequence and add the delay. Same registers and
same mask (mpll-rst bits 4/6/7 == the vendor's mpll-sel-syscon 0xd0), so the
end state is unchanged; only the ordering and the settle time differ.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-normal.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-normal.c b/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-normal.c
index be1fffd04..281836552 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-normal.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/sprd-hwdvfs-normal.c
@@ -2827,12 +2827,14 @@ static int sprd_cpudvfs_common_init(struct cpudvfs_archdata *pdev)
 	}
 
 	for (ix = 0; ix < pdev->mpll_num; ++ix) {
-		ret = pdev->phy_ops->mpll_relock_enable(pdev, ix, true);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
-		ret = pdev->phy_ops->mpll_pd_enable(pdev, ix, true);
-		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+		/*
+		 * Hand the MPLL output over to DVFS control before enabling
+		 * auto relock and auto power down. The vendor 5.4 driver
+		 * (sprd_mpll_output_source_switch) does the switch first and
+		 * waits for the analog side to settle; doing it afterwards
+		 * leaves the frequency-update state machine parked, so the
+		 * clock never leaves its TWPLL boot parent.
+		 */
 		addr = pdev->mplls[ix].anag_reg;
 		bit = (1 << pdev->mplls[ix].POST_DIV) |
 		      (1 << pdev->mplls[ix].ICP) |
@@ -2844,6 +2846,16 @@ static int sprd_cpudvfs_common_init(struct cpudvfs_archdata *pdev)
 			return ret;
 		}
 
+		/* Wait for the analog configuration to finish */
+		udelay(50);
+
+		ret = pdev->phy_ops->mpll_relock_enable(pdev, ix, true);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		ret = pdev->phy_ops->mpll_pd_enable(pdev, ix, true);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
 		/* Need to init mpll index table if necessary */
 		ret = pdev->phy_ops->mpll_index_table_init(pdev, ix);
 		if (ret)
